{"abstract":"Skipping of BRCA2 exon 3 (∆E3) is a naturally occurring splicing event, complicating clinical classification of variants that may alter ∆E3 expression. This study used multiple evidence types to assess pathogenicity of 85 variants in/near BRCA2 exon 3. Bioinformatically predicted spliceogenic variants underwent mRNA splicing analysis using minigenes and/or patient samples. ∆E3 was measured using quantitative analysis. A mouse embryonic stem cell (mESC) based assay was used to determine the impact of 18 variants on mRNA splicing and protein function. For each variant, population frequency, bioinformatic predictions, clinical data, and existing mRNA splicing and functional results were collated. Variant class was assigned using a gene-specific adaptation of ACMG/AMP guidelines, following a recently proposed points-based system. mRNA and mESC analysis combined identified six variants with transcript and/or functional profiles interpreted as loss of function. Cryptic splice site use for acceptor site variants generated a transcript encoding a shorter protein that retains activity. Overall, 69/85 (81%) variants were classified using the points-based approach. Our analysis shows the value of applying gene-specific ACMG/AMP guidelines using a points-based approach and highlights the consideration of cryptic splice site usage to appropriately assign PVS1 code strength.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Thomassen, Mads","Mesman, Romy L S","Hansen, Thomas V O","Menendez, Mireia","Rossing, Maria","Esteban-Sánchez, Ada","Tudini, Emma","Törngren, Therese","Parsons, Michael T","Pedersen, Inge Sokilde","Teo, Soo Hwang","Kruse, Torben A","Møller, Pål","Borg, Åke","Jensen, Uffe Birk","Christensen, Lise Lotte","Singer, Christian F","Muhr, Daniela","Santamarina, Marta","Brandao, Rita","Andresen, Brage Storstein","Feng, Bing-Jian","Canson, Daffodil","Richardson, Marcy E","Karam, Rachid","Pesaran, Tina","LaDuca, Holly","Conner, Blair R","Abualkheir, Nelly","Hoang, Lily","Calléja, Fabienne M G R","Andrews, Lesley","James, Paul A","Bunyan, Dave","Hamblett, Amanda","Radice, Paolo","Goldgar, David E","Walker, Logan C","Engel, Christoph","Claes, Kathleen B M","Macháčková, Eva","Baralle, Diana","Viel, Alessandra","Wappenschmidt, Barbara","Lazaro, Conxi","Vega, Ana","Consortium, Enigma","Vreeswijk, Maaike P G","de la Hoya, Miguel","Spurdle, Amanda B"],"cuid":["S04-099.93-005252"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["ENIGMA consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Spurdle, Amanda B.","Thomassen, Mads"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Belgium","Czechia","Germany","Italy","Malaysia","Netherlands","New Zealand","Norway","Singapore","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ambry Genetics","Cancer Research Malaysia","Carlos III Health Institute (ISCIII) (CIBER)","Catalan Institute of Oncology-ICO","Center for Biomedical Network Research on Rare Diseases (CIBERER)","Complutense University of Madrid","Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Nazionale dei Tumori","German Sport University Cologne","Ghent University","Ghent University Hospital","Hospital Clínico San Carlos de Madrid","IRCCS Centro di Riferimento Oncologico - Aviano PN","IRCCS Fondazione Istituto Nazionale per lo studio e la cura dei tumori - Milano","Institute Catala Oncologia","Instituto de Salud Carlos III","Leiden University","Leiden University Medical Center","Leipzig University","Lund University","L’Hospitalet de Llobregat","Maastricht University","Maastricht University Medical Centre+","Masaryk Memorial Cancer Institute","Medical University of Vienna","Middlesex Health","National Cancer Centre","Nelune Comprehensive Cancer Care Centre","Oslo University Hospital","Peter Maccallum Cancer Centre","Prince of Wales Hospital","QIMR Berghofer Medical Research